> Don't use magic markers to write scrolls of identify. Identify,
> enchant weapon, and light are the three most common scrolls, and as
> such, you'll get *scads* of them through polypiling. If you have a ton
> of unihorns (at least 8), and around 20 "junk" scrolls, a wand of
> polymorph is well worth a wish. Basically, try to fill out the gaps in
> your ascension kit via polypiling, and then wish for anything else you
> need.

Thanks -- this is really good advice.  I thought that I had more, but
it turns out that I have 8 unicorn horns total, which conservatively
leaves me with 6 to polypile I guess.  I probably come up a bit short
with junk scrolls, although it depends on the interpretation of "junk"
I guess.  The major problem here is that I did not do a good job early
on planning to polypile eventually, and didn't realize how valuable
every item potentially is, even junk items.  Looks like it's time to
visit my minetown stash and see what I left there -- I think that
there are some scrolls and cursed rings there.

> Good stuff to polypile:
> 0. Rings and amulets.
> The *best* polyfodder. You'll generate enough ?identify through
> polypiling to identify these as you create them.
> 1. unicorn horns for magic markers. Preferably blessed and in piles of
> *no more than four*.
> 2. Piles of no more than four (blessed scrolls) - if you have more
> than four objects in a pile, or cursed objects, there's an increased
> chance of items disappearing.
> 3. Elven cloaks/elven boots - the lightest and most common "magical
> armor". Magical armor includes all the nice stuff such as speed boots
> and gauntlets of power.
> For the most part, if you *want* magical armor from polypiling, you
> need elven cloaks, elven boots, and junk such as fumble boots
> (cancelled first), because nonmagical armor almost never polypiles
> into magical stuff.
> 4. blessed fixed greased +7 darts/arrows. Far less necessary than 1 or
> 2, but if you [n]ame all the darts in a pile different stuff, you'll
> get tons of +7 weapons. You can get a stack of daggers *and* a +7
> silver saber this way.
>
> Don't stack 20 scrolls or 20 potions or 20 comestibles up in the same
> pile - distribute them to avoid creation of golems.

